{"sections":[{"image":"ic_component_intro.png","chapter":"Use of first components provided by OUDS","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26","title":"Use your first OUDS components","kind":"hero","backgroundImage":"ic_component_intro.png","estimatedTimeInMinutes":30,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS provides components ready to be used, specified in Figma assets and preventing users to handle tokens."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are rendered thanks to the theme in use."}]}]},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"stepsSection":[{"code":"tutorial-3-1.swift","type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"First, prepare the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ContentView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by adding inside it a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScrollView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"caption":[],"runtimePreview":null},{"code":"tutorial-3-2.swift","type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Now, let’s add radio buttons to let the user choose its gender.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The official components are ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSRadio","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSRadioItem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but the package has also a ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSRadioPicker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to implement quicky a group of radios.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This component can be replaced by your own.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The radio picker is defined by an array of values to display radio items associated to a tag, i.e. an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" thing shared through a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Inside a picker the user can select only one value, not zero.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add such picker with three items inside.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":"tutorial-3-2.png"},{"code":"tutorial-3-3.swift","type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The radio picker is alone, it is the time to add below a checkbox. OUDS provides two components: ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSCheckbox","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" which is a simple checkbox, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSCheckboxItem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" which is a checkbox (duh!) with additional texts and icons.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The state of the checkbox is shared through a boolean ","type":"text"},{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In some cases you may need to use ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSCheckboxIndeterminate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSCheckboxItemIndeterminate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if you want a three-states checkbox.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a checkbox item with only two states.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":"tutorial-3-3.png"},{"code":"tutorial-3-4.swift","type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There are also components who do not have any behaviors and are here only for visual rendering, for example dividers which can be horizontal or vertical.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A divider is, in the end, a stroke with a color. You will see later, colors in OUDS have two values: a light mode value, and a dark mode value. Here the divider can have a color which can change, or not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Choose to add an instance of ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSHorizontalDivider","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":"tutorial-3-4.png"},{"code":"tutorial-3-5.swift","type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With radio and checkbox, OUDS provides also switch elements (toggles). They can be alone (","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSSwitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or with texts (","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSSwitchItem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Just like the checkbox, the switch exposes its state through a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a switch item, it will be used as a trick to force the change of the color scheme for the view for our future operations.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You will then be able to see the automatic changes of colors when you switch the color scheme.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":"tutorial-3-5.png"},{"code":"tutorial-3-6.swift","type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Users may need to navigate outside the app, like, for example, opening a website. Thus the ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSLink","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" component can be integrated. It can be only with a text or also a chevron indicator.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add an ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSLink","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the app and make it open the iOS documentation OUDS website.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":"tutorial-3-6.png"},{"code":"tutorial-3-7.swift","type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the end, we can also add a button. Button are one of the most used components in an app and bring a lof of the power and the style of the brand.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You can find it with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSButton","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Such button has an appearance changing its colors, and also a style (loading or not).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Thanks to the theme, the enabled, disabled, hover, focus or pressed states are managed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Let’s add a button with some rules: if checkbox is not checked it is disabled. When tapped, change the style of the button during 5 seconds.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":"tutorial-3-7.png"}],"title":"Add basic components","anchor":"Add-basic-components","contentSection":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"We will work on a kind of formular using main OUDS components.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Feel free to style and design things as you want.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia"}]}]},{"kind":"assessments","anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding","assessments":[{"title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the developer using OUDS component need to manage the look and feel of the components?"}]}],"type":"multiple-choice","content":[],"choices":[{"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No! The components use the design specifications, i.e. tokens, thanks to the theme, to define the style they must have in all cases.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":false},{"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That is the reason why the ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSThemeableView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is so important: it injects the theme as environment variable so that any component can get it to define its style.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":true}]}]},{"kind":"callToAction","title":"Add more OUDS components","featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Components can be similar to iOS native components, or can also be original and strongly related to Orange Unified Design System needs."}],"action":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-4-use-other-components","type":"reference","overridingTitle":"Get started","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get started"}]}}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-3-use-first-components"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents","doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/$volume","doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Use-of-first-components-provided-by-OUDS"]],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents","modules":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Import-of-the-Swift-Package-and-choose-its-librairies","projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies#Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessment"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Preparation-of-the-theme","projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-2-instanciate-theme#Basic-structure-for-the-app","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-2-instanciate-theme#Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessment"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-2-instanciate-theme"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Use-of-first-components-provided-by-OUDS","projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-3-use-first-components#Add-basic-components","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-3-use-first-components#Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessment"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-3-use-first-components"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Richer-and-more-original-components-of-OUDS","projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-4-use-other-components#Add-basic-components","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-4-use-other-components#Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessment"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-4-use-other-components"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Typography,-view-modifiers-and-tokens","projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-5-styling-things#Use-of-tokens","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-5-styling-things#Use-of-view-modifiers","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-5-styling-things#Final-result","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-5-styling-things#Want-to-be-an-artist","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-5-styling-things#Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessment"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-5-styling-things"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Go-further-with-more-ressources","projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-6-going-further#More-resources","kind":"task"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-6-going-further"}]}]},"metadata":{"category":"Orange Unified Design System","role":"project","categoryPathComponent":"Table-Of-Contents","title":"Use your first OUDS components"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-3-use-first-components"},"kind":"project","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-3-use-first-components#Check-Your-Understanding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-3-use-first-components#Check-Your-Understanding","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Check Your Understanding"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-3-use-first-components#Check-Your-Understanding","type":"link","title":"Check Your Understanding"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents/Use-of-first-components-provided-by-OUDS":{"type":"topic","title":"Use of first components provided by OUDS","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Use-of-first-components-provided-by-OUDS","url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents\/use-of-first-components-provided-by-ouds","abstract":[],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-2-instanciate-theme":{"type":"topic","title":"Instanciate and inject a theme","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-2-instanciate-theme","url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-2-instanciate-theme","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The theme is exposed as one object which will be injected inside your SwiftUI view."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The theme provides all tokens which defines in the end the rendering of everything."}],"estimatedTime":"15min","kind":"project","role":"project"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies#Check-Your-Understanding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies#Check-Your-Understanding","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Check Your Understanding"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies#Check-Your-Understanding","type":"link","title":"Check Your Understanding"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-2-instanciate-theme#Basic-structure-for-the-app":{"type":"section","title":"Basic structure for the app","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-2-instanciate-theme#Basic-structure-for-the-app","url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-2-instanciate-theme#Basic-structure-for-the-app","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The theme is exposed as one object which will be injected inside your SwiftUI view."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The theme provides all tokens which defines in the end the rendering of everything."}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"tutorial-3-3.swift":{"highlights":[{"line":20},{"line":23},{"line":24},{"line":25},{"line":26},{"line":27},{"line":28},{"line":29}],"type":"file","identifier":"tutorial-3-3.swift","fileName":"Content.swift","content":["\/\/","\/\/ Software Name: OUDS iOS","\/\/ SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) Orange SA","\/\/ SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT","\/\/","\/\/ This software is distributed under the MIT license,","\/\/ the text of which is available at https:\/\/opensource.org\/license\/MIT\/","\/\/ or see the \"LICENSE\" file for more details.","\/\/","\/\/ Authors: See CONTRIBUTORS.txt","\/\/ Software description: A SwiftUI components library with code examples for Orange Unified Design System","\/\/","","import OUDSSwiftUI","import SwiftUI","","struct ContentView: View {","","    @State var selectedGender: Genders = .male","    @State var termsAccepted: Bool = false","","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            OUDSRadioPicker(selection: $selectedGender,","                            radios: genderRadioValues(),","                            placement: .horizontal(false))","","            OUDSCheckboxItem(isOn: $termsAccepted, label: \"I accept the terms of use\")","        }","    }","","    \/\/ MARK: - Utils","","    enum Genders: String, Hashable {","        case male","        case female","        case nonBinary","    }","","    func genderRadioValues() -> [OUDSRadioPickerData<Genders>] {","        [","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.male, label: \"Mr\"),","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.female, label: \"Ms\"),","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.nonBinary, label: \"Other\"),","        ]","    }","}"],"fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift"},"ic_component_intro.png":{"identifier":"ic_component_intro.png","alt":"OUDS components logo","type":"image","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/OUDSThemesContract\/ic_component_intro.png","traits":["1x","light"]}]},"tutorial-3-4.swift":{"highlights":[{"line":28},{"line":29}],"type":"file","identifier":"tutorial-3-4.swift","fileName":"Content.swift","content":["\/\/","\/\/ Software Name: OUDS iOS","\/\/ SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) Orange SA","\/\/ SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT","\/\/","\/\/ This software is distributed under the MIT license,","\/\/ the text of which is available at https:\/\/opensource.org\/license\/MIT\/","\/\/ or see the \"LICENSE\" file for more details.","\/\/","\/\/ Authors: See CONTRIBUTORS.txt","\/\/ Software description: A SwiftUI components library with code examples for Orange Unified Design System","\/\/","","import OUDSSwiftUI","import SwiftUI","","struct ContentView: View {","","    @State var selectedGender: Genders = .male","    @State var termsAccepted: Bool = false","","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            OUDSRadioPicker(selection: $selectedGender,","                            radios: genderRadioValues(),","                            placement: .horizontal(false))","","            OUDSHorizontalDivider(color: .brandPrimary)","","            OUDSCheckboxItem(isOn: $termsAccepted, label: \"I accept the terms of use\")","        }","    }","","    \/\/ MARK: - Utils","","    enum Genders: String, Hashable {","        case male","        case female","        case nonBinary","    }","","    func genderRadioValues() -> [OUDSRadioPickerData<Genders>] {","        [","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.male, label: \"Mr\"),","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.female, label: \"Ms\"),","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.nonBinary, label: \"Other\"),","        ]","    }","}"],"fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift"},"tutorial-3-1.swift":{"highlights":[{"line":25},{"line":26},{"line":27}],"type":"file","identifier":"tutorial-3-1.swift","fileName":"Tutorial.swift","content":["import OUDSSwiftUI","import SwiftUI","","\/\/ MARK: - App","","@main","struct OUDSTutorialSandboxApp: App {","    ","    let myTheme = OrangeTheme()","    ","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            OUDSThemeableView(theme: myTheme) {","                ContentView()","            }","        }","    }","}","","\/\/ MARK: - Tutorial Content View","","struct ContentView: View {","    ","    var body: some View {","        ScrollView {","            Text(\"Hello OUDSThemesContract!\")","        }","    }"],"fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift"},"tutorial-3-6.swift":{"highlights":[{"line":23},{"line":24},{"line":36},{"line":37},{"line":38},{"line":39}],"type":"file","identifier":"tutorial-3-6.swift","fileName":"Content.swift","content":["\/\/","\/\/ Software Name: OUDS iOS","\/\/ SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) Orange SA","\/\/ SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT","\/\/","\/\/ This software is distributed under the MIT license,","\/\/ the text of which is available at https:\/\/opensource.org\/license\/MIT\/","\/\/ or see the \"LICENSE\" file for more details.","\/\/","\/\/ Authors: See CONTRIBUTORS.txt","\/\/ Software description: A SwiftUI components library with code examples for Orange Unified Design System","\/\/","","import OUDSSwiftUI","import SwiftUI","","struct ContentView: View {","","    @State var selectedGender: Genders = .male","    @State var termsAccepted: Bool = false","    @State var switchToDarkMode: Bool = false","","    @Environment(\\.openURL) var openUrl","","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            OUDSRadioPicker(selection: $selectedGender,","                            radios: genderRadioValues(),","                            placement: .horizontal(false))","","            OUDSHorizontalDivider(color: .brandPrimary)","","            OUDSCheckboxItem(isOn: $termsAccepted, label: \"I accept the terms of use\")","","            OUDSSwitchItem(\"Switch to dark mode\", isOn: $switchToDarkMode)","","            OUDSLink(text: \"Go to the website\", indicator: .next) {","                openUrl.callAsFunction(URL(string: \"https:\/\/ios.unified-design-system.orange.com\")!)","            }","        }.preferredColorScheme(switchToDarkMode ? .dark : .light)","    }","","    \/\/ MARK: - Utils","","    enum Genders: String, Hashable {","        case male","        case female","        case nonBinary","    }","","    func genderRadioValues() -> [OUDSRadioPickerData<Genders>] {","        [","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.male, label: \"Mr\"),","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.female, label: \"Ms\"),","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.nonBinary, label: \"Other\"),","        ]","    }","}"],"fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift"},"tutorial-3-5.png":{"identifier":"tutorial-3-5.png","alt":"A radio picker, an horizontal divider, a checkbox item and a switch item","type":"image","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-3-5.png","traits":["1x","light"]}]},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-5-styling-things#Check-Your-Understanding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-5-styling-things#Check-Your-Understanding","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Check Your Understanding"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-5-styling-things#Check-Your-Understanding","type":"link","title":"Check Your Understanding"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-4-use-other-components#Check-Your-Understanding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-4-use-other-components#Check-Your-Understanding","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Check Your Understanding"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-4-use-other-components#Check-Your-Understanding","type":"link","title":"Check Your Understanding"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies":{"type":"topic","title":"Swift Package integration","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies","url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS iOS is exposed through an open source Swift Package hosted on GitHub, and provides several librairies for your needs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"These librairies help to split products and make users able to select only what they need."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI is the only official supported framework."}],"estimatedTime":"10min","kind":"project","role":"project"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-3-use-first-components#Add-basic-components":{"type":"section","title":"Add basic components","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-3-use-first-components#Add-basic-components","url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-3-use-first-components#Add-basic-components","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS provides components ready to be used, specified in Figma assets and preventing users to handle tokens."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are rendered thanks to the theme in use."}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-5-styling-things#Use-of-view-modifiers":{"type":"section","title":"Use of view modifiers","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-5-styling-things#Use-of-view-modifiers","url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-5-styling-things#Use-of-view-modifiers","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Even if components increase the identity of your apps, it is not enough. Typography, fonts and tokens are here to improve that."}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents":{"type":"topic","title":"Swift Package iOS Tutorial","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents","url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Discovering a new framework can be exciting and scary. Learn how you can embed and use OUDS Swift Package."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"With this tutorial you will learn fundamental concepts of Orange Unified Design System and discover the layers of this framework."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Theme, components, tokens… everything will be introduced!"}],"kind":"overview","role":"overview"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-6-going-further#More-resources":{"type":"section","title":"More resources","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-6-going-further#More-resources","url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-6-going-further#More-resources","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Since you have learnt how OUDS works with theme, themeable view, components, tuning and vieww modifiers, it is time now to discover some online resources."}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"tutorial-3-5.swift":{"highlights":[{"line":21},{"line":32},{"line":33},{"line":34}],"type":"file","identifier":"tutorial-3-5.swift","fileName":"Content.swift","content":["\/\/","\/\/ Software Name: OUDS iOS","\/\/ SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) Orange SA","\/\/ SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT","\/\/","\/\/ This software is distributed under the MIT license,","\/\/ the text of which is available at https:\/\/opensource.org\/license\/MIT\/","\/\/ or see the \"LICENSE\" file for more details.","\/\/","\/\/ Authors: See CONTRIBUTORS.txt","\/\/ Software description: A SwiftUI components library with code examples for Orange Unified Design System","\/\/","","import OUDSSwiftUI","import SwiftUI","","struct ContentView: View {","","    @State var selectedGender: Genders = .male","    @State var termsAccepted: Bool = false","    @State var switchToDarkMode: Bool = false","","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            OUDSRadioPicker(selection: $selectedGender,","                            radios: genderRadioValues(),","                            placement: .horizontal(false))","","            OUDSHorizontalDivider(color: .brandPrimary)","","            OUDSCheckboxItem(isOn: $termsAccepted, label: \"I accept the terms of use\")","","            OUDSSwitchItem(\"Switch to dark mode\", isOn: $switchToDarkMode)","        }.preferredColorScheme(switchToDarkMode ? .dark : .light)","    }","","    \/\/ MARK: - Utils","","    enum Genders: String, Hashable {","        case male","        case female","        case nonBinary","    }","","    func genderRadioValues() -> [OUDSRadioPickerData<Genders>] {","        [","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.male, label: \"Mr\"),","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.female, label: \"Ms\"),","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.nonBinary, label: \"Other\"),","        ]","    }","}"],"fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries":{"type":"section","title":"Import the Swift Package and the libraries","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries","url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-1-package-and-librairies#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS iOS is exposed through an open source Swift Package hosted on GitHub, and provides several librairies for your needs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"These librairies help to split products and make users able to select only what they need."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI is the only official supported framework."}],"kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents/Preparation-of-the-theme":{"type":"topic","title":"Preparation of the theme","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Preparation-of-the-theme","url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents\/preparation-of-the-theme","abstract":[],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents/Typography,-view-modifiers-and-tokens":{"type":"topic","title":"Typography, view modifiers and tokens","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents\/Typography,-view-modifiers-and-tokens","url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents\/typography,-view-modifiers-and-tokens","abstract":[],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"tutorial-3-3